From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ville Takio <ville+git@takio.fi>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 04:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: b43: N-PHY: receive A-MPDUs of up to 64 KiB

846 advertises 32 KiB, the firmware's default M_MIMO_MAXSYM. With a
two-stream client that limits how much it sends per TXOP, which costs
most on a busy channel.

On the RT-AC56U's BCM43217 (firmware 784.2) b43 has 0x8000 in
M_MIMO_MAXSYM and 5 in M_WATCHDOG_8TU; wl 7.14.164 on the same chip
has 0xffff and 10, brcmsmac's values for a 64 KiB factor. Write those
on N-PHY and advertise 64 KiB there.

OnePlus Nord 2 (2x2) uplink, TCP, -37 dBm, channel 6, alternating
modules: 69.7 Mbit/s mean over 7 runs against 66.0 over 4 without
(wl: ~75). The phone's bytes per TXOP (bytes received / CTS sent) go
from about 24 kB to 28-31 kB, like wl's 28 kB. Channel 1 and the
downlink are unchanged within the noise; one RX FIFO 1 overflow in
four 20 s uplinks.

Signed-off-by: Ville Takio <ville+git@takio.fi>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/b43.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/b43.h
@@ -332,6 +332,8 @@ enum {
 #define  B43_SHM_SH_UCODESTAT_SUSP	3	/* suspended */
 #define  B43_SHM_SH_UCODESTAT_SLEEP	4	/* asleep (PS) */
 #define B43_SHM_SH_MAXBFRAMES		0x0080	/* Maximum number of frames in a burst */
+#define B43_SHM_SH_MIMO_MAXSYM		0x00BA	/* Longest PSDU received, N-PHY (bytes) */
+#define B43_SHM_SH_WATCHDOG_8TU		0x003C	/* RX A-MPDU watchdog (8 TU); was DEFAULTIV */
 #define B43_SHM_SH_SPUWKUP		0x0094	/* pre-wakeup for synth PU in us */
 #define B43_SHM_SH_PRETBTT		0x0096	/* pre-TBTT in us */
 /* SHM_SHARED tx iq workarounds */
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
@@ -5861,6 +5861,16 @@ static int b43_wireless_core_init(struct
 	 * a timeout, so we never send any probe resp.
 	 * A timeout of zero is infinite. */
 	b43_shm_write16(dev, B43_SHM_SHARED, B43_SHM_SH_PRMAXTIME, 1);
+	/*
+	 * Receive A-MPDUs of up to 64 KiB on N-PHY, as brcmsmac does for
+	 * that factor: the longest PSDU to 64 KiB and its watchdog to 10.
+	 */
+	if (dev->phy.type == B43_PHYTYPE_N) {
+		b43_shm_write16(dev, B43_SHM_SHARED, B43_SHM_SH_MIMO_MAXSYM,
+				0xFFFF);
+		b43_shm_write16(dev, B43_SHM_SHARED, B43_SHM_SH_WATCHDOG_8TU,
+				10);
+	}
 
 	b43_rate_memory_init(dev);
 	b43_set_phytxctl_defaults(dev);
@@ -6501,6 +6511,9 @@ static void b43_ht_cap_set_chains(struct
 
 	if (rx_ss >= 2)
 		ht_cap->mcs.rx_mask[1] = 0xff;
+	/* The firmware takes up to 64 KiB, see b43_wireless_core_init() */
+	if (dev->phy.type == B43_PHYTYPE_N)
+		ht_cap->ampdu_factor = IEEE80211_HT_MAX_AMPDU_64K;
 	if (tx < 2)
 		ht_cap->cap &= ~IEEE80211_HT_CAP_TX_STBC;
 	if (tx_ss != rx_ss)
